{"from": "passage:lk-20-47", "type": "parallels", "to": "passage:mt-23-13", "note": "the WEB prints the 'devour widows' houses' woe at Matt 23:13 (traditional numbering 23:14), so the join follows the WEB verse; mt-23-14 keeps the א B omission variant (reviewer 5's mk-12-40 fix mirrored for Luke)"}
{"from": "text:talmud-sanhedrin-41a", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-20-20-spies-governor-authority", "grade": "D", "note": "Reception text: 'forty years before the destruction of the [Second] Temple, capital punishment ceased in Israel' (traditionally c. 28 CE), because 'the Sanhedrin required the approbation of the Roman procurator of Judea before they could punish any malefactor by death'. Redacted c. 500 CE, so it may not describe the 30s CE exactly; it reports the tradition of Roman-governor control of capital jurisdiction."}
{"from": "text:talmud-sanhedrin-41a", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikipedia-capital-punishment-judaism"}
{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-199-sanhedrin", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:lk-20-20-spies-governor-authority", "grade": "B", "note": "Ananus assembled the sanhedrim and stoned James while the procurator Albinus was on the road, and 'it was not lawful for Ananus to assemble a sanhedrim without his consent' (62 CE) - in this period Judean authorities acted under the Roman governor's authority, the jurisdiction Luke's trap presupposes. It attests the setting, not that spies were sent."}
{"from": "claim:lk-20-20-spies-governor-authority", "type": "documented_by", "to": "source:wikisource-ant20"}
{"from": "claim:lk-20-20-spies-governor-authority", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-22-16-pharisees-herodians", "note": "Luke has spies pretending to be righteous, sent to deliver him to the governor's authority; Matthew has the Pharisees' disciples sent together with the Herodians, with no governor mentioned."}
{"from": "claim:lk-20-34-36-marriage-resurrection", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:mt-22-24-levirate-marriage", "note": "Luke alone expands the answer: those worthy of that age neither marry nor die any more, being like the angels; Matthew 22:30 and Mark 12:25 give only 'neither marry nor are given in marriage'."}
{"from": "claim:lk-20-20-spies-governor-authority", "type": "mentions", "to": "person:pontius-pilate"}
